+ "gaps": [
+  "Only one Lagoa-headquartered AI company is confirmed so far (Strong Answer, from its own page). SPIC, a firm building the AI.EVENT audience-sentiment platform, is described by RTP as based in Loulé, while a Jornal do Algarve article we could not open (403) is reported by a search summary to place it in Lagoa: left out until its registered town is confirmed, and passed to the Loulé site's agent as a lead. Sources to look for next: the Portuguese company registers by municipality code, the Balcão do Empreendedor, LinkedIn company pages.",
+  "The newest Lagoa AI news we have is from December 2025, plus the February 2026 hackathon in the events list. No Lagoa AI news dated after February 2026 has been found yet.",
+  "Lagoa's council news feed carries no AI items at all in its latest 25 entries (up to 13 November 2026): the council's own AI work is reported by regional press, not by the council.",
+  "Two Lagoa stories fail the PrompTugal test as written and stay out: the City as a Platform innovation prize (March 2025, sensors and data, AI not mentioned) and the Ferragudo augmented reality portal (April 2026, AI not mentioned).",
+  "Left out as not AI: the council's WhatsApp channel for residents and visitors (Barlavento, 28 July 2026), which is part of the council's digital transformation strategy but where no AI or chatbot is mentioned. Search results also mix in AI courses held in Lagoa on the island of São Miguel in the Azores, a different municipality that we do not cover.",
+  "Postal do Algarve could not be read (it shows a bot check), so its Lagoa coverage is missing. Sul Informação refused automated reads. The date of the CCDR report is the meeting date, the report itself was published later in 2025.",
+  "The talk on a large language model solution for the Algarve's municipalities is only a title in a programme: we found no later report of it being built or used.",
+  "Starting a company here is only partly mapped: the council's entrepreneurship pages name a support office, an online desk and a Fábrica do Empreendedor but publish no grants, incentives, incubator details or steps, and its 'support measures' and 'co-financed projects' menu links were empty when read. Investors, local talent and cooperatives in Lagoa are not mapped yet."
+ ],
+ "voice": {
+  "lede": "Ó pá, Lagoa: sun, wine, a sea cave with a hole in its roof, and now a council that asks the robots about the air.",
+  "mandate": "PrompTugal.news Lagoa: AI and technology in Lagoa, the land of tourists, wine and congresses, where the council and the parishes got to the robots before the companies did, and what reaches us from the Algarve, Portugal and the world. Independent, and every fact has its source, pois.",
+  "gravity": "Lagoa lives on tourism, with wine (a Lagoa DOC), a fishing past in Ferragudo, Carvoeiro and Benagil, and a growing business of congresses and events. Its AI is mostly public-sector: the council runs a Smart City portal and an IT team that has been working on AI with data-protection and processing limits in mind, and one parish has put an AI assistant on its website. In the private sector we have confirmed one Lagoa IT firm that sells AI agents, and a British school that hosted a teenagers' AI hackathon in February 2026, ó pá, not bad for a land of beaches.",
+  "gaps_intro": "Here is what we could not find, and yes, we looked behind the fishing boats too."
+ },
