-    "text": "Vila Real de Santo António is a planned town on the Guadiana, built from 1773 on a grid and completed in 1776, whose old fishing and canning economy gave way to tourism, with many residents working across the river around Ayamonte in Spain. Today it is pushing to become a national pole of the blue economy, around its fishing port and a shipbuilding yard, and it is wiring its historic centre under the PRR-funded VRSA Digital project and joining a six-municipality PRR sensor platform. It shares the Eurocidade do Guadiana with Ayamonte and Castro Marim, and the council holds its presidency in 2026. We found no AI company based in the town yet, so for now the AI story is a shipyard that built a robot test vessel and plans a unit for unmanned vessels, data groundwork and a Spanish neighbour's plans.",
